\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Schematic for gearboxes as an analogy for wind-driven vehicles. (a) Positive transmission for downwind motion, where the input from the wheels (analogous to Rack 1) results in a faster output at the propeller (Rack 2). (b) Negative transmission for upwind motion, where an idler gear reverses the direction of motion.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gearboxes}{{2}{3}{Schematic for gearboxes as an analogy for wind-driven vehicles. (a) Positive transmission for downwind motion, where the input from the wheels (analogous to Rack 1) results in a faster output at the propeller (Rack 2). (b) Negative transmission for upwind motion, where an idler gear reverses the direction of motion}{figure.2}{}}
